= Commons =

== Overview ==
'''Commons''' is a shared resource or resource system governed, used, or accessed by a community or multiple participants under some set of formal or informal rules.

Many classic commons problems concern common-pool resources: resources from which exclusion is difficult while one participant's extraction subtracts from what remains for others.

A commons is not defined by inevitable collapse. Empirical institutional research shows that communities can sometimes govern shared resources sustainably through boundaries, monitoring, graduated sanctions, conflict-resolution processes, nested institutions, and locally adapted rules.

Digital and knowledge commons may differ because information can be largely non-rival even when infrastructure, attention, moderation, or funding remain scarce.

== Boundaries ==
* commons ≠ public good
* commons ≠ unowned resource by definition
* commons ≠ inevitable tragedy

